<title>UK: UK's AEA buying Hyprotech for 34 mln stg.</title>
<headline>UK's AEA buying Hyprotech for 34 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>British science and nuclear technology group AEA Technology Plc said on Thursday that it is buying Canadian process simulation software company Hyprotech Ltd for 34 million stg.  </p>
<p>AEA said the payment will be partly funded by the placing of 6.4 million new AEA shares at a price of 404p per share. Cazenove is broker to the placing.</p>
<p>The balance of 8.1 million pounds will be funded from additional borrowings.</p>
<p>&quot;This acquisition is in line with our strategy of seeking profitable growth,&quot; said AEA chief executive Peter Watson.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
